### Sprint v0.11.0: Repair MVP

**Recommended sprint theme:** Catalog repair and integrity recovery.

The Repair MVP (items 1330–1337) is a coherent 7-item suite with a clear internal dependency chain, real user value (recovering from corrupted or missing Parquet fragments), and no dependency on any other open work. It is the most cohesive unit of work in the backlog right now and should ship as a single sprint.

#### Sprint Table

| ID | Title | Priority | Sequencing |
|----|-------|----------|------------|
| 1330 | repair.py module skeleton + bth repair CLI wiring | **P1** | First — all others depend on this |
| 1331 | Cool-tier sentinel cleanup: auto-delete .tmp, quarantine stale .bak | **P1** | After 1330; simplest repair action, validates the scaffold |
| 1332 | Corrupt fragment quarantine: move unreadable .parquet to quarantine | **P1** | After 1330; pairs naturally with 1331 |
| 1333 | Pre-rebuild warm backup + --acknowledge-warm-loss gate | **P1** | After 1330; safety gate before any destructive warm rebuild |
| 1336 | Warm-to-cool re-export: recover run records from warm DB when cool fragments missing | **P2** | After 1333 (backup must exist before re-export can be safe) |
| 1337 | Archive-tier repair: quarantine-and-log SHA256 mismatches in cold archive | **P2** | After 1330; independent of warm path |
| 1335 | Test suite for repair MVP: fixture-driven, 5 repair actions + dry-run | **P1** | Runs in parallel with implementation; gate before PR |
| 1334 | MCP mirror: mcp__bathos__repair tool | **P2** | After all repair actions implemented and tested |

**Dependency chain:**
```
1330 (skeleton)
  ├── 1331 (sentinel cleanup)
  ├── 1332 (corrupt quarantine)
  ├── 1337 (archive SHA256 quarantine)
  └── 1333 (warm backup gate)
        └── 1336 (warm-to-cool re-export)

1335 (tests) — developed alongside all of the above
1334 (MCP mirror) — final, after all actions pass tests
```

